Henry traveled 20 miles before his first stop.

## Step 2: Calculate the distance traveled after the second stop
Henry's second stop was 15 miles before the end of the trip, so he traveled 60 - 15 = 45 miles after the second stop.

## Step 3: Determine the distance between the first and second stops
To find the distance between his first and second stops, subtract the distance traveled before the first stop (20 miles) from the distance traveled after the second stop (45 miles). distance_between_stops = 45 - 20 = 25

